 "read_this_first": "The step named last time as the next gain without a model, a better choice among the learner's candidates, was built and did not gain. An order counted from further experience (on 64 bugs whose fixes are known: how often an operator of a given kind, with so many lessons behind it and so many candidates, holds the published fix) has the published fix among the first 200 candidates for 18 of those 64 bugs, each ordered with the counts of the other 63. The learner's own order by votes has it there for 20. The rule written down before the bugs were ordered said: if the counted order does not have it there for more bugs, the 100 scored bugs are not touched. They were not. No test was run for this record: it is about where the published fix stands, not about repairs. One run, one machine, by the producer; nobody else has re-run it.",
